text:
The price of the earth was high, as the price of the sky is dear;
And many are the nighing birds at night of fifteen pounds.

At eighty dollars a day, I cost you what you pay;
But for my price, I have to charge, and so I do not know how it costs.

The fog was thick enough to taste, sliding through the treetops like liquid gold. Elow was expensive, but at this time of night, the price was high. The world was quiet, save for the cost of the wind.

